{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795693500,"nonce":"nyH2EnBHW9d4gC7a2BEXnE7K6g8=","title":"The desktop and web audio controls differ","message":"audio_player() uses MediaControls on desktop (play button, time, seek bar of two elements, volume as a percentage) and the video controls on the web (mute button, volume bar, drawn seek bar). The audio-player page of the website says its live demo uses the same controls as the native preview, which the preview picture shows to be untrue.\n\nEither the audio widget uses one set on both, which changes the CSS classes that style it, or the page text changes.\n\nLeft over from ef459cd31f89aea2193a5a1201996bbc768aa18832f5850b06a8b0c876197d3a.","files":null}]}